CHECKPASS(1)                User Commands

NAME
    checkpass - check the password of the caller

SYNOPSIS
    checkpass

DESCRIPTION
    checkpass reads one line, the password, and compares it with the
    password of the account of the real user id. It reads from the
    terminal without echo, or from standard input when that is not a
    terminal. checkpass is installed set user id root. Only root may read
    /etc/shadow. A wrong password costs two seconds before checkpass
    exits.

EXIT STATUS
    0 for the right password, 1 for a wrong one and 2 for an error.

SEE ALSO
    lock(1), passwd(1)
